>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Chips</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Meta and Nvidia</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">What Meta is buying from Nvidia. Rack figures are on <a href="/ai/hardware/chips/blackwell/">Blackwell</a> and <a href="/ai/hardware/chips/rubin/">Rubin</a>. The other suppliers are on the <a href="/ai/hardware/chips/meta/">Meta stack</a>.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Millions of GPUs</h2>
    <p>On 17 February 2026 Nvidia said the Meta partnership deploys CPUs and millions of Blackwell and Rubin GPUs, including GB300-based systems. Blackwell is the generation in those racks now. Rubin is the next Nvidia family in the same agreement.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Grace, then Vera</h2>
    <p>Nvidia calls the Grace CPU piece the first large-scale Grace-only deployment. Vera CPUs have the potential for large-scale deployment in 2027. That 2027 line is a potential deployment, not a shipped count.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/meta-builds-ai-infrastructure-with-nvidia">NVIDIA, 17 February 2026</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
